looking back at the weirdest and  riskiest movies of 2019 some were  fantastic and others just didn't work  either way these films featured plots  that left viewers scratching their heads  here are some of the most baffling  movies of 2019 heads up some light  spoilers ahead writer-director re asters  midsummer avoids many horror tropes to  tell its tale of full core and Florence  Pugh is nothing short of a powerhouse in  the lead role mid Samar is one of those  films where you can tell things are  going to go majorly sideways from the  beginning aster loves to leave dangling  threads for his characters and his  audience to pull on with lots of half  answers sprinkled throughout sans fun  regardless of what your theory is about  the movie might be there are most likely  clues to support them and plenty of  clues that point in the opposite  direction  velvet buzzsaw is one of those movies  that makes it tough to truly tell  whether what you're watching is actually  any good it has all the pieces in place  starting with a solid cast led by Jake  Gyllenhaal and Rene Russo Dan Gilroy  directed it fresh off the dark and  grossly satisfying Nightcrawler it  centers around artwork coming to life  and murdering critics and that basically  sums things up on the other hand is  anything in velvet buzzsaw really  happening or is it all just an extremely  meta commentary on the way we consume  and critique art what's even going on in  this movie there are a lot of questions  raised and not a lot of answers given  but if you like watching good actors  playing bizarre characters velvet  buzzsaw is for you very few directors  have debuted with their first feature  quite like Jordan Peele did with 27  teens get out he had high hopes to live  up to with the sophomore effort us and  he delivered another fresh thriller with  a ton of layers if you want to get crazy  it didn't quite strike the same nerve as  get-out but it inspired plenty of hot  takes on its release everyone in the  main cast plays a double role in the  film their regular selves and their  tethered version Unleashed from the  secret underground society where they've  been kept for who knows how long as the  film goes on and you learn more about  what the tethered are it becomes  apparent why they're a force to be  reckoned with Lupita Nyong'o steals the  show delivering an impressive dual  performance even after you've seen it  multiple times us will keep you guessing  and have you theorizing for hours Robert  Eggers followed up as 2015 film the  witch with 29 teens equally perplexing  the lighthouse it's shot in black and  white and an almost square aspect ratio  no widescreen here  it's a two-man show with Robert  Pattinson and Willem Dafoe playing - men  manning a lighthouse together and it's  completely bizarre when you watch the  lighthouse there are about 50 different  ways to interpret it maybe everything is  literally happening maybe some of it is  maybe Pattinson isn't real  maybe Dafoe isn't unlike the witch the  lighthouse never really gives you any  answers still it's an impressive film  that a group of people could watch at  the same time and all come to wildly  different plausible conclusions the  perfection is a body horror masterpiece  that will have you squirming in your  seat it's also a film that will keep you  guessing until the very end even if  things do wrap up a little more neatly  than many of 2019 s weirdest films the  plot centers around two women in a  prestigious music academy what starts as  a simple tale of revenge becomes more  and more insane it's exploitative and  tough to watch but it definitely hits  the right buttons for people who are  looking for a bizarre viewing experience  something is wrong something is wrong  with me featuring killer performances  from both allison williams and logan  browning the perfection is creepy weird  and oddly satisfying one of the best  films of 2019 is also one of its most  baffling legendary korean director bong  Joon hos parasite is full of twists and  turns and you never quite know exactly  where it's going the film starts out as  a commentary on wealth and social class  and a story in which one lower-class  family begins to push themselves into  the life and social standing of a much  wealthier family about halfway through  however things take a dramatic turn and  parasite becomes more of a horror  thriller as secrets are revealed and a  series of dramatic revelations occur  joon-ho employs dark humour so perfectly  that it keeps you off balance while  watching parasite you never know if you  should be smiling or just plain  horrified not every baffling movie of  2019 was good and serenity never quite  gels that said it's still worth a watch  just for one particularly memorable and  bizarre plot twist if you want to see  Matthew McConaughey and Anne Hathaway  work their way through some truly  strange material serenity is a good way  to do it  after Hathaway's character asks her  ex-husband played by McConaughey to  murder her current husband he wrestles  with the idea and you'll probably think  you know where this plot is going from  there fun fact you don't when the twist  arrives odds are pretty good that you'll  find it just doesn't work that well but  man does it try serenity really swings  for the fences and many of the bizarre  plot twists further confuse things  rather than clearing them up check out  one of our newest videos right here plus  even more looper videos about your  favorite stuff are coming soon subscribe  to our YouTube channel and hit the belt  so you don't miss a single one
 

